@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Help & FAQ";
}

<div class="content-page">
    <p class="page-eyebrow">Help &amp; FAQ</p>
    <h1>A few helpful answers</h1>
    <p class="lead">Got a question? Check out the FAQ!</p>

    <section class="faq-list" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
        <details open>
            <summary>How do I get my daily calorie target?</summary>
            <p>
                Complete your <a asp-page="/Profile/Index">Profile</a>. You can use the calculated estimate
                based on your details, activity and goal, or enter a custom target.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>Where do foods come from?</summary>
            <p>
                You can create custom foods or search USDA FoodData Central. Nutrition for USDA results is
                resolved by the server before a food is logged. Check any value that matters to you because
                external and user-entered data can contain mistakes.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>What are portions?</summary>
            <p>
                Portions let you save familiar amounts such as a slice or bowl against a custom food. You can
                still log an exact mass or volume whenever you prefer.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>Will editing a food change old Diary entries?</summary>
            <p>
                No. Diary entries snapshot the food name, serving basis, nutrition and portion description
                used when you logged them, so your history remains intact if the original food changes later.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>How do themes and Capy customisation work?</summary>
            <p>
                Open <a asp-page="/Customisation">Customise Capy</a> to equip owned cosmetics and choose Light,
                Dark or System theme. Signed-in theme choices are saved to your profile; signed-out choices use
                this browser.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>What if I cannot confirm my email or sign in?</summary>
            <p>
                Use <a asp-area="Identity" asp-page="/Account/ResendEmailConfirmation">Resend email confirmation</a>
                or <a asp-area="Identity" asp-page="/Account/ForgotPassword">reset your password</a>. If you use
                two-factor authentication and cannot access your authenticator, use one of your saved recovery codes.
            </p>
        </details>

        <details id="nutrition-estimates" open>
            <summary>Are calorie and nutrition figures medical advice?</summary>
            <p>
                No. Calorie, TDEE and nutrition figures are estimates for general information and tracking.
                Food values may come from your input or an external data source and may be inaccurate. Do not
                rely on the app as medical advice. If you have medical or specialised dietary needs—including
                pregnancy, an eating disorder, or a condition affected by nutrition—seek advice from an
                appropriately qualified professional.
            </p>
        </details>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-4">
        Still stuck? <a asp-page="/Feedback">Send feedback</a>. Please do not include passwords, recovery codes,
        medical details or other sensitive information.
    </p>
</div>
